WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.658
An acquisition.

2
00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:04.160
A funding round.

3
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.662
A restructuring.

4
00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:07.893
The numbers have been checked.

5
00:00:07.943 --> 00:00:10.272
The contracts have been checked.

6
00:00:10.322 --> 00:00:13.469
But can the team actually deliver the plan?

7
00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:16.869
That is what Human Due Diligence looks at.

8
00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:22.455
It is a process in two phases,
with a hard decision point in between.

9
00:00:22.505 --> 00:00:25.289
Phase one examines the team dynamic.

10
00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:30.720
Every member of the team completes
the team scan and the energy scan.

11
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:38.907
That gives you the picture at team level: collaboration,
energy balance, and the spread between members.

12
00:00:38.957 --> 00:00:42.219
That is where the first decision is made.

13
00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:46.258
If there are dysfunctional signals, it stops here.

14
00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:49.732
If there are none, the second phase begins.

15
00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:54.982
With one central question:
can this team deliver on its ambition?

16
00:00:55.032 --> 00:00:58.779
The platform advises, the organisation decides.

17
00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:01.528
Phase two is an in-depth analysis.

18
00:01:01.578 --> 00:01:12.445
For each key individual: the talent pattern, the drivers, an indication
of cognitive capacity, and the complementarity within the team.

19
00:01:12.495 --> 00:01:20.827
At the end there is a well-founded judgement,
with the risks stated and with the questions that remain open.

20
00:01:20.877 --> 00:01:25.871
In two reports: one for whoever decides,
one for the team itself.

21
00:01:26.139 --> 00:01:27.664
No diagnosis.

22
00:01:27.764 --> 00:01:29.701
No selection decision.

23
00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.882
The organisation is the one who decides.

